WEBVTT

00:00:07.883 --> 00:00:09.356
SETH: Dude, where's Tim?

00:00:09.406 --> 00:00:13.700
SAM: He's in Rome. His church took a trip to go see the Pope.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:20.552
MATT: Lucky. The most exciting thing my church ever did was a bake sale where Mrs. Henderson's brownies put three people in the hospital.

00:00:20.602 --> 00:00:22.650
SETH: Did Tim at least bring us anything?

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.714
SAM: He texted us a picture of the Pope waving.

00:00:25.764 --> 00:00:29.876
MATT: That's it? I wanted a souvenir. Like a holy water squirt gun.

00:00:29.926 --> 00:00:36.624
SAM: Guys, did you see the news? Clara Powers is coming to North Park tomorrow. For a campaign rally.

00:00:36.674 --> 00:00:41.987
SETH: Clara Powers? The First Lady? The senator? She's running for president?

00:00:42.037 --> 00:00:44.398
SAM: Yeah. Against Henry Reyes.

00:00:44.448 --> 00:00:52.452
MATT: Henry Reyes is the coolest guy alive. He wears sunglasses indoors. At night. At funerals.

00:00:52.502 --> 00:01:00.114
SETH: My mom watched Clara's Address to the Nation. It was supposed to be fifteen minutes. It's still going.

00:01:00.164 --> 00:01:02.029
SAM: That was in September.

00:01:02.079 --> 00:01:06.373
SETH: Mom fell asleep on the couch. We just put a blanket on her and let the TV run.

00:01:06.423 --> 00:01:08.602
MATT: We should go to her rally.

00:01:08.652 --> 00:01:11.040
SAM: Why would we go to her rally?

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:13.399
MATT: To troll her. Obviously.

00:01:13.449 --> 00:01:14.478
SETH: ...I'm in.

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:23.681
SAM: Okay. Every politician reads off a teleprompter. Every single one.

00:01:23.731 --> 00:01:29.044
SETH: My cousin runs the sound and screens at the community center. He owes me twenty bucks.

00:01:29.094 --> 00:01:31.142
MATT: So we hack the teleprompter.

00:01:31.192 --> 00:01:35.643
SAM: We don't hack it. We just plug in my laptop and type whatever we want.

00:01:35.693 --> 00:01:38.159
SETH: Dude, that's literally hacking.

00:01:38.209 --> 00:01:42.974
MATT: And I'm bringing an air horn. Every time she says "unprecedented," I blast it.

00:01:43.024 --> 00:01:45.464
SAM: She's gonna say it like forty times.

00:01:45.514 --> 00:01:47.849
MATT: That's why I bought the big air horn.

00:01:55.487 --> 00:02:03.830
CLARA POWERS: Thank you, North Park! Thank you! Please, sit down. Get comfortable. Really comfortable. Use the restroom now if you need to.

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:13.608
CLARA POWERS: Before I begin, I want to acknowledge that this gym sits on the ancestral land of the North Park Elks Lodge parking lot.

00:02:13.658 --> 00:02:15.497
SAM: She hasn't even started yet.

00:02:15.547 --> 00:02:25.275
CLARA POWERS: I also want to acknowledge this podium. Its pronouns are wood and oak, and it deserves our respect.

00:02:25.325 --> 00:02:27.765
MATT: She's talking to the furniture, dude.

00:02:27.815 --> 00:02:30.594
CLARA POWERS: These are unprecedented times—

00:02:32.544 --> 00:02:37.100
CLARA POWERS: —truly unprecedented, deeply unprecedented—

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:44.141
CLARA POWERS: —and I am SO glad to see this much energy in the room!

00:02:44.191 --> 00:02:46.082
SETH: She thinks we're cheering.

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:58.629
CLARA POWERS: When I'm president, every child in America will get a feelings counselor. And every feelings counselor gets a feelings counselor. It's counselors all the way down, North Park!

00:02:58.679 --> 00:03:00.936
MATT: Who counsels the last counselor?

00:03:00.986 --> 00:03:02.224
SAM: Taxes.

00:03:02.274 --> 00:03:10.095
CLARA POWERS: I will raise taxes on billionaires, millionaires, thousandaires, and anyone running a lemonade stand that turns a profit.

00:03:10.145 --> 00:03:11.697
SETH: Hey! That's me!

00:03:11.747 --> 00:03:21.031
CLARA POWERS: And I'm proposing a federal ban on gas stoves, gas cars, and gas. Beans included.

00:03:21.081 --> 00:03:23.286
MATT: She's coming for the chili, dude.

00:03:29.027 --> 00:03:41.237
CLARA POWERS: ...which is why my fourteen-point plan is actually thirty-eight points, and point nineteen has its own sub-points, which I will now read in full—

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:42.995
SAM: Now. Do it now.

00:03:47.945 --> 00:03:56.602
CLARA POWERS: And in conclusion, I, Clara Powers, admit that... Henry Reyes is way cooler than me.

00:03:57.852 --> 00:04:02.146
CLARA POWERS: And I smell like... old soup.

00:04:03.996 --> 00:04:11.713
CLARA POWERS: My husband Justin only married me because I wouldn't stop talking until he said yes.

00:04:11.763 --> 00:04:14.516
CLARA POWERS: ...Wait. Who wrote this?

00:04:18.966 --> 00:04:24.932
CLARA POWERS: Don't clap for that! Stop clapping! This is UNPRECEDENTED!

00:04:31.582 --> 00:04:33.134
HENRY REYES: Evening, North Park.

00:04:33.184 --> 00:04:36.094
SETH: Holy crap. It's Henry Reyes.

00:04:36.144 --> 00:04:41.692
HENRY REYES: Heard there was a rally going on. Heard it three hours ago. From Ohio. You could hear it from Ohio.

00:04:41.742 --> 00:04:47.186
CLARA POWERS: Henry. This is MY event. I have this room booked until Thursday.

00:04:47.236 --> 00:04:49.284
HENRY REYES: Clara, it's Tuesday.

00:04:49.334 --> 00:04:51.225
CLARA POWERS: Exactly.

00:04:51.275 --> 00:04:52.722
HENRY REYES: You boys do this?

00:04:52.772 --> 00:04:54.846
MATT: ...No.

00:04:54.896 --> 00:05:01.202
HENRY REYES: Shame. Best speech she ever gave. Short, honest, and somebody else wrote it.

00:05:01.252 --> 00:05:08.446
CLARA POWERS: Fine. I am going to say something I have never said before in my entire life.

00:05:08.496 --> 00:05:10.048
HENRY REYES: Here it comes.

00:05:10.098 --> 00:05:12.512
CLARA POWERS: ...No comment.

00:05:15.562 --> 00:05:16.800
SAM: She stopped.

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:18.715
SETH: She actually stopped talking.

00:05:18.765 --> 00:05:24.653
HENRY REYES: Ladies and gentlemen, that's what we call a miracle. Tim's gonna be mad he went to Rome for the wrong one.

00:05:24.703 --> 00:05:29.128
CLARA POWERS: Actually, if you'll allow me to elaborate on "no comment"—

00:05:29.178 --> 00:05:31.043
HENRY REYES: Boys. Air horn.

00:05:37.976 --> 00:05:39.867
SETH: You know, I learned something today.

00:05:39.917 --> 00:05:40.894
SAM: What?

00:05:40.944 --> 00:05:48.190
SETH: Democracy only works when everybody gets a chance to be heard.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.217
MATT: Yeah.

00:05:49.267 --> 00:05:51.237
SETH: But not for four hours.

00:05:51.287 --> 00:05:56.052
MATT: Oh, Tim texted. He said the Pope saw us on the news.

00:05:56.102 --> 00:05:58.281
SAM: Really? What'd the Pope say?

00:05:58.331 --> 00:06:00.823
MATT: "Amen."
